---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

import { getAllPosts } from '../../lib/posts';

const allPosts = await getAllPosts();

const englishReviews = allPosts.filter(
  (post) => post.type === 'review' && post.language === 'en'
);

const englishNews = allPosts.filter(
  (post) => post.type === 'news' && post.language === 'en'
);
---

<BaseLayout
  reviews={englishReviews}
  news={englishNews}
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Information on the processing of personal data of users who visit Retro-Gamers.it."
  image="/og-image.jpg"
  canonical="https://www.retro-gamers.it/en/privacy-policy/"
  lang="en"
>
  <main class="legal-page">
    <div class="container">

      <section class="legal-hero">
        <span>Privacy</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>
          Information on the processing of personal data of users who visit
          Retro-Gamers.it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <article class="legal-content">

        <p class="legal-updated">
          Last updated: April 28, 2026
        </p>

        <h2>1. Data controller</h2>

        <p>
          The data controller is Marco Finelli, responsible for the Retro-Gamers.it
          editorial project.
        </p>

        <p>
          For any privacy-related request, you can write to:
          <a href="mailto:guybrush@retro-gamers.it">guybrush@retro-gamers.it</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. What data we process</h2>

        <p>
          When browsing Retro-Gamers.it, technical and browsing data may be processed,
          such as IP address, browser information, device used, pages visited, date
          and time of access, and technical data required for the website to function.
        </p>

        <p>
          The website currently does not provide contact forms, newsletters, user
          accounts or restricted areas. Therefore, personal data is not collected
          directly through forms filled in by users.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Purposes of processing</h2>

        <p>
          Data may be processed for the following purposes:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>to allow the correct technical operation of the website;</li>
          <li>to ensure security, maintenance and prevention of abuse;</li>
          <li>to measure visits and understand how content is used;</li>
          <li>to display embedded content from external platforms, such as YouTube;</li>
          <li>to manage external links and affiliate links to third-party platforms.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Legal basis</h2>

        <p>
          Technical processing required for the operation of the website is based on
          the legitimate interest of the controller in keeping the website secure,
          accessible and functional.
        </p>

        <p>
          Processing related to non-essential analytics tools and third-party content,
          such as Google Analytics or embedded YouTube videos, is carried out only
          after the user’s consent, when required by applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Hosting and infrastructure services</h2>

        <p>
          Retro-Gamers.it is hosted through Vercel. Vercel may process technical data
          required for the delivery, security and operation of the website.
        </p>

        <p>
          The website may use Vercel Web Analytics to obtain aggregate visit
          statistics. According to Vercel’s documentation, Web Analytics does not use
          third-party cookies and identifies visits through a hash generated from the
          request, with sessions discarded after 24 hours.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Google Analytics</h2>

        <p>
          Retro-Gamers.it may use Google Analytics to collect statistics on website
          usage. Google Analytics may involve the processing of browsing data and the
          use of cookies or similar technologies.
        </p>

        <p>
          Google Analytics is loaded only after the user has consented to the
          “Analytics” category through the consent management system available on the
          website.
        </p>

        <h2>7. Embedded YouTube content</h2>

        <p>
          Some articles may include videos embedded from YouTube. Viewing such content
          may involve the transfer of data to Google/YouTube and the use of cookies
          or similar technologies by third parties.
        </p>

        <p>
          When possible, Retro-Gamers.it uses more privacy-conscious embedding modes,
          such as the youtube-nocookie.com domain. In any case, embedded videos are
          loaded only after the user has consented to third-party content.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Amazon, eBay and other affiliate links</h2>

        <p>
          Some articles may contain affiliate links to Amazon, eBay or other external
          websites. If the user makes a purchase through these links, Retro-Gamers.it
          may receive a small commission, at no additional cost to the user.
        </p>

        <p>
          By clicking an affiliate link, the user leaves Retro-Gamers.it and accesses
          a third-party website. From that moment, the processing of personal data is
          governed by the privacy policy and cookie policy of the destination website.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Social networks and external links</h2>

        <p>
          The website contains links to Retro-Gamers.it social profiles, such as
          Facebook, Instagram and X. These links lead to external platforms, which
          process data according to their own policies.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Data retention</h2>

        <p>
          Technical and browsing data is retained for the time necessary for the
          purposes for which it is collected, including security, maintenance,
          aggregate statistics and technical or legal obligations.
        </p>

        <p>
          Cookie consent preferences may be stored in the user’s browser to avoid
          showing the banner repeatedly.
        </p>

        <h2>11. User rights</h2>

        <p>
          Within the limits provided by Regulation EU 2016/679, the user may request
          access, rectification, erasure, restriction, objection to processing and
          portability of personal data.
        </p>

        <p>
          To exercise these rights, you can write to:
          <a href="mailto:guybrush@retro-gamers.it">guybrush@retro-gamers.it</a>.
        </p>

        <p>
          The user also has the right to lodge a complaint with the Italian Data
          Protection Authority.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Changes to this policy</h2>

        <p>
          This Privacy Policy may be updated over time, including as a result of
          technical, legal or editorial changes to the website.
        </p>

      </article>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>